00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.340
Here is how it works when the contract is a game rather than a news event.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:05.860
A sportsbook posts a number and takes the other side.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:08.660
An exchange contract does not work that way.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.740
2 traders agree a price.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.320
If the event happens, the buyer is paid a fixed sum.

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:17.060
If it does not, the seller keeps the price.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.340
The venue need not hold a view.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.120
The last trade is the number.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:26.740
If the other side is a pool, a formula and a pile of collateral set that number instead.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:32.540
A 2021 paper in the Journal of Finance uses liquid sports betting contracts to test

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:33.540
pricing anomalies.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.020
Two features matter.

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:41.060
There is no systematic risk of the equity kind, and the payoff is fixed outside the betting itself.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:50.660
That setup dodges the joint hypothesis problem, so a gap between the traded price and the later result can be called mispricing rather than pay for risk.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:55.780
The author finds strong momentum, the pattern fits delayed over reaction.

00:07:56.420 --> 00:08:00.220
It does not fit under reaction, and it does not fit rational pricing.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:05.620
The returns are a fraction of what financial markets pay, and they do not clear transaction

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.960
costs, so arbitrage does not wipe the streak out.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:14.820
A pattern from that betting record also predicts value and momentum returns in US equities.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.120
That finding is a description of old betting books.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:23.240
It is not a method to copy, and it is not a verdict on any live contract.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.540
A 2023 paper on archive looks at the pool design.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:34.520
It argues an automated market maker built like Uniswap is not lined up with fair odds, so liquidity

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:41.520
providers hold a risk the formula never priced. The authors describe UBET's UAMM, smart contracts

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:47.780
meant to set sports prices inside collateral pools, and they report experiments with positive outcomes.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:54.400
That is a design result, not a forecast scorecard. Read a sports contract price as a trade

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.300
or as a formula's output, not as a house line and not as a settled chance.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:05.840
The Journal of Finance Result says those trades can keep a momentum streak that costs make hard to trade away.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.300
A thin book is a weaker version of the same object.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.000
Those papers measure prices and liquidity.

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:17.700
They do not measure gambling harm, which is a different question from whether the last trade knew something.

